          "literatureReview": "Renal Function Tests (RFTs) are essential blood tests that evaluate kidney function by measuring waste products and electrolytes in the blood. The kidneys filter waste products from the blood and maintain the body's fluid and electrolyte balance. Abnormal RFT results can indicate kidney disease, dehydration, urinary tract obstruction, or other conditions affecting kidney function. Regular monitoring of renal function is important for patients with diabetes, hypertension, or known kidney disease."
